WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.691 --> 00:00:18.193
Dolittle and the animals missed Polynesia and Chee-Chee very much.

2
00:00:19.113 --> 00:00:23.174
But they knew Polynesia and Chee-Chee were happier in Africa.

3
00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:25.355
"Where are we now, Dr.

4
00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:27.535
Dolittle?" asked Dab-Dab.

5
00:00:27.555 --> 00:00:30.573
"I'm not sure," Dr.

6
00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:32.114
Dolittle scratched his head.

7
00:00:32.134 --> 00:00:35.737
"Dr. Dolittle!

8
00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:37.478
Dr. Dolittle!"

9
00:00:38.279 --> 00:00:40.121
Voices were calling from the sky.

10
00:00:40.141 --> 00:00:42.042
"Oh, hello!"

11
00:00:42.663 --> 00:00:44.444
the doctor waved to some birds.

12
00:00:44.464 --> 00:00:46.926
"You're going the wrong way!"

13
00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.247
one shouted.

14
00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:50.789
"These are Barbary waters!"

15
00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.511
another one said.

16
00:00:52.531 --> 00:00:56.935
"Barbary? What's that?"

17
00:00:57.535 --> 00:00:58.316
asked the doctor.

18
00:00:59.084 --> 00:01:01.846
"They're pirates," the other bird whispered.

19
00:01:02.607 --> 00:01:04.848
Dab-Dab began to shake with fear.

20
00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.270
"Pirates? Oh, no!"

21
00:01:08.511 --> 00:01:09.712
he quacked loudly.

22
00:01:09.732 --> 00:01:15.596
"The Barbary pirates wait for boats," explained the bird.

23
00:01:15.616 --> 00:01:19.098
"After they attack the boat, they steal everything in it."

24
00:01:19.118 --> 00:01:23.041
"The pirates take people, too," said another bird.

25
00:01:23.061 --> 00:01:26.263
"Sometimes, they throw people into the water!"

26
00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.490
Dr. Dolittle did not want to meet any pirates.

27
00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:33.211
"Go this way!

28
00:01:33.511 --> 00:01:34.492
You'll be safe!"

29
00:01:35.152 --> 00:01:36.112
the birds cried out.

30
00:01:36.693 --> 00:01:39.895
So the doctor sailed the boat away from the Barbary waters.

31
00:01:39.915 --> 00:01:43.357
"Whew! That was close!"

32
00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.938
Dr. Dolittle wiped his forehead.

33
00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:48.660
The next day, Dr.

34
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.342
Dolittle forgot all about the Barbary pirates.

35
00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:58.625
"Mmmm I smell roast beef Jip was talking in his sleep.

36
00:01:59.465 --> 00:02:00.966
Dr. Dolittle laughed.

37
00:02:03.387 --> 00:02:09.409
"Apple pie potatoes and Jip mumbled.

38
00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.931
"Yummy! I smell roast beef!"

39
00:02:13.511 --> 00:02:14.831
Gub-Gub said happily.

40
00:02:16.612 --> 00:02:18.513
Dr. Dolittle sniffed the air.

41
00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:21.954
"Jip smells roast beef, too."

42
00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.775
"Maybe it's from that ship!"

43
00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:26.176
Gub-Gub pointed.

44
00:02:27.276 --> 00:02:31.078
"Uh, Doctor," Dab-Dab's voice shook.

45
00:02:31.098 --> 00:02:33.699
"Dogs have a good sense of smell.

46
00:02:34.159 --> 00:02:37.100
Almost as good as pigs," Gub-Gub said.

47
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:44.343
"Dr. Dolittle uh Dab-Dab pointed but couldn't speak.

48
00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.624
"What is it, Dab-Dab?"

49
00:02:47.124 --> 00:02:48.365
Dr. Dolittle asked.

50
00:02:49.725 --> 00:02:51.146
Jip was still sleeping.

51
00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:56.476
"Trouble, bad men.

52
00:02:56.496 --> 00:03:04.282
I smell five, no, six men grrrrrr," he growled.

53
00:03:05.122 --> 00:03:07.604
Then he barked so loudly he woke up.

54
00:03:09.605 --> 00:03:12.247
"I had a terrible dream.

55
00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:14.048
I Dr.

56
00:03:14.128 --> 00:03:16.630
Dolittle!" Jip suddenly jumped up.

57
00:03:17.591 --> 00:03:20.673
A big ship with red sails was coming toward them.

58
00:03:20.693 --> 00:03:26.605
"It's the Barbary pirates," whispered Dab-Dab.

59
00:03:30.346 --> 00:03:32.107
Dr. Dolittle gave orders.

60
00:03:32.607 --> 00:03:35.988
"We must put more sails on our boat," he shouted.

61
00:03:36.008 --> 00:03:37.809
"Jip! Gub-Gub!

62
00:03:38.289 --> 00:03:39.630
Find all the sails.

63
00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:41.350
Bring them to me!"

64
00:03:42.011 --> 00:03:44.892
The pirate ship moved closer and closer.

65
00:03:47.173 --> 00:03:49.974
Dr. Dolittle used every sail on the boat.

66
00:03:50.654 --> 00:03:52.955
But the boat was still not fast enough.

67
00:03:52.975 --> 00:03:54.716
"What do we do?"

68
00:03:55.264 --> 00:03:56.145
cried Gub-Gub.

69
00:03:56.165 --> 00:03:58.586
"Too-Too! Find the birds!"

70
00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.888
Dr. Dolittle told the owl.

71
00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.211
Too-Too came back with two birds.

72
00:04:06.031 --> 00:04:07.673
"Only two birds?"

73
00:04:08.173 --> 00:04:08.813
barked Jip.

74
00:04:09.454 --> 00:04:10.474
"The rest are coming!"

75
00:04:11.095 --> 00:04:12.236
one bird called down.

76
00:04:12.256 --> 00:04:14.357
"Bring all the rope you have.

77
00:04:14.637 --> 00:04:17.099
Quickly!" shouted the other one.

78
00:04:19.521 --> 00:04:21.262
Dr. Dolittle brought the rope.

79
00:04:21.742 --> 00:04:25.397
"Make the rope into a lot of thin strings," said one bird.

80
00:04:26.157 --> 00:04:28.378
Soon they had hundreds of thin strings.

81
00:04:29.039 --> 00:04:31.460
Dr. Dolittle tied the ends to the boat.

82
00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:32.921
"Now what?"

83
00:04:33.481 --> 00:04:34.382
he asked the bird.

84
00:04:36.483 --> 00:04:38.884
Suddenly the sky started to get dark.

85
00:04:39.525 --> 00:04:41.426
There was a low rumbling sound.

86
00:04:41.446 --> 00:04:43.767
"What's that noise?"

87
00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.168
Gub-Gub asked.

88
00:04:45.188 --> 00:04:48.350
"I don't know," Jip replied.

89
00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.051
He did not push the pig away this time.

90
00:04:51.071 --> 00:04:52.452
"Look up there!"

91
00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.781
Too-Too shouted excitedly.

92
00:04:55.502 --> 00:04:58.143
Above them hundreds of birds covered the sky.

93
00:05:01.325 --> 00:05:03.247
Each bird took a piece of string.

94
00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:04.888
"Okay, everyone!

95
00:05:05.248 --> 00:05:05.928
Hang on!"

96
00:05:06.709 --> 00:05:07.610
said a little bird.

97
00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.371
Together, the birds pulled the strings.

98
00:05:11.132 --> 00:05:13.774
Dr. Dolittle's boat nearly flew in the air.

99
00:05:14.694 --> 00:05:16.836
It moved faster than the pirates' ship.

100
00:05:19.678 --> 00:05:23.120
All the animals, except Dab-Dab, began to laugh.

101
00:05:23.724 --> 00:05:26.528
"Yippee! This is fun!"

102
00:05:26.948 --> 00:05:27.729
shouted Jip.

103
00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:30.332
"Look! I'm flying!"

104
00:05:30.773 --> 00:05:31.654
cried Gub-Gub.

105
00:05:32.335 --> 00:05:34.918
Shortly, the red sails disappeared.
